on the streets of New Delhi Sarah P  Shrivastav is on a mission  she's asking young women like herself to  stop and think about their sexual health  therapy herself was forced to reckon  with the issue when she went to a  gynecologist to ask for contraceptive  called an intrauterine device or IUD the  gynecologist asked her if she already  had children and if her husband was with  her when should be told the doctor that  she was unmarried she was turned away  she outright denied it and she said that  no it's not safe for you and when I  asked for evidence to prove that she  didn't really have anything to say so I  think again it was very driven by  societal attitudes around who can get an  IUD who is supposed to use contraception  who should be having sex is should we  having sex after being denied by another  doctor so he gave up but she doesn't  want other women too when it comes to  women's health in India authorities are  focused on improving health care for  mothers but a group of young women have  come together to say that their access  to sexual health should not be denied  simply because they're unmarried  they're calling the campaign health over  stigma sex before marriage  look commonly discussed in popular  culture and social media is still a  taboo in India and this often shows in  the attitudes of doctors the campaign is  appealing to medical authorities  hospitals and doctors to sign their code  of conduct and provide non-judgmental  services to all women equally as an  unmarried woman if I go up to the doctor  the doctor shouldn't ask me questions  like are you married or you know like  like do your parents know you know like  things like that so when they go to the  doctor so my confidentiality should be  maintained like I should've been scared  to go to the doctor and the campaign is  resonating with some we live in a  society where where our sexuality is  somehow very much repressed and also  suppressed so I think it is high time  when time to come direct face to face  and have a dialogue about how sexuality  has a role in our lives  sexual hygiene and sexual or matters are  something which are being hidden meaning  that they are not much spoken out stuff  that many people are resistant talking  about these things I think these issues  must be of you know taken up  already Delhi's Medical Council has  agreed to hear the troops petition as  more women join the movement they are  hopeful they can change attitudes across  the country
 

